WEBVTT

00:00:00.332 --> 00:00:00.994
Grid Bot

00:00:00.994 --> 00:00:04.074
Builder. Grid Bot Blueprint. Lesson one.

00:00:04.626 --> 00:00:08.615
Introduction. Education only. Not

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:09.339
financial

00:00:09.339 --> 00:00:12.061
advice. This is general information and

00:00:12.061 --> 00:00:14.264
doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:17.343
financial situation or needs. Crypto is

00:00:17.343 --> 00:00:19.928
high risk. You could lose all the money

00:00:19.928 --> 00:00:20.112
you

00:00:20.112 --> 00:00:20.295
put

00:00:20.295 --> 00:00:23.583
in. Crypto carries a risk of total loss.

00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:27.206
The prices are public historical daily

00:00:27.206 --> 00:00:29.915
closes, marked Example. A close is the

00:00:29.915 --> 00:00:33.553
last price of the day. Past performance is

00:00:33.553 --> 00:00:35.619
not a reliable indicator of future

00:00:35.619 --> 00:00:39.209
results. A grid bot places waiting buy

00:00:39.209 --> 00:00:41.810
orders on lines below the price and sell

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:44.411
orders on lines above it, inside a top and

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:47.092
a bottom you choose. The space between

00:00:47.092 --> 00:00:47.332
your

00:00:47.332 --> 00:00:47.511
top

00:00:47.511 --> 00:00:47.691
and

00:00:47.691 --> 00:00:47.931
your

00:00:47.931 --> 00:00:48.291
bottom

00:00:48.291 --> 00:00:48.410
is

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:48.770
called

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:48.950
the

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:52.451
band. A limit order is an order that waits

00:00:52.451 --> 00:00:52.593
at

00:00:52.593 --> 00:00:55.311
a price you choose. It does not chase the

00:00:55.311 --> 00:00:58.945
price. The sells above need some coin, so

00:00:58.945 --> 00:01:01.280
a grid starts with part cash and part

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.459
coin, and that is a description, not

00:01:03.459 --> 00:01:06.337
advice about what to hold. Cash is money

00:01:06.337 --> 00:01:06.731
you can

00:01:06.731 --> 00:01:10.498
spend. Coin is the crypto. A stop is a

00:01:10.498 --> 00:01:12.633
rule you write down before you start,

00:01:12.633 --> 00:01:14.697
saying what you will do if the price

00:01:14.697 --> 00:01:16.904
leaves the band and does not come back.

00:01:18.104 --> 00:01:20.752
When a chart says Example, it means a real

00:01:20.752 --> 00:01:22.999
past price used as an example, not a

00:01:22.999 --> 00:01:26.498
forecast. By the end you will know what a

00:01:26.498 --> 00:01:30.675
grid bot places. You will see that idea on

00:01:30.675 --> 00:01:34.690
one real path from 2023. You will be able

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:34.819
to

00:01:34.819 --> 00:01:35.013
say

00:01:35.013 --> 00:01:35.466
the stop

00:01:35.466 --> 00:01:35.724
rule

00:01:35.724 --> 00:01:35.854
in

00:01:35.854 --> 00:01:36.048
one

00:01:36.048 --> 00:01:39.108
sentence. Think of a ladder leaned on a

00:01:39.108 --> 00:01:41.438
wall. The rungs wait, and they do not

00:01:41.438 --> 00:01:41.766
chase

00:01:41.766 --> 00:01:44.528
you. The ladder is the analogy, and the

00:01:44.528 --> 00:01:48.062
chart beside it is the real past path. The

00:01:48.062 --> 00:01:50.111
range is the top line and the bottom

00:01:50.111 --> 00:01:51.313
line, copied from the

00:01:51.313 --> 00:01:53.819
path. Every close in this window stayed

00:01:53.819 --> 00:01:54.549
between those

00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:54.731
two

00:01:54.731 --> 00:01:58.155
lines. The range is a top and a bottom you

00:01:58.155 --> 00:02:00.987
draw before any rung. Without a top and a

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:01.390
bottom,

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:02.465
you can't place the

00:02:02.465 --> 00:02:06.350
lines. Six equal gaps of about 900 dollars

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.942
sit between the bottom line and the top

00:02:08.942 --> 00:02:12.210
line. Seven lines make those six gaps. A

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:13.190
limit order waits

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:13.321
on

00:02:13.321 --> 00:02:13.386
a

00:02:13.386 --> 00:02:15.894
level. It does not run after the price.

00:02:16.944 --> 00:02:17.513
The levels

00:02:17.513 --> 00:02:18.018
are limit

00:02:18.018 --> 00:02:18.650
orders that

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:18.903
wait

00:02:18.903 --> 00:02:19.029
on

00:02:19.029 --> 00:02:19.219
the

00:02:19.219 --> 00:02:22.381
rungs. A limit order sits at a price. It

00:02:22.381 --> 00:02:25.969
does not chase. A fence has a top rail and

00:02:25.969 --> 00:02:28.832
a bottom rail. Inside them, the price can

00:02:28.832 --> 00:02:31.608
wander. On the chart those rails are the

00:02:31.608 --> 00:02:34.809
bottom line and the top line. The daily

00:02:34.809 --> 00:02:35.483
close is the

00:02:35.483 --> 00:02:36.224
last price of

00:02:36.224 --> 00:02:36.427
the

00:02:36.427 --> 00:02:39.340
day. Crypto trades all day, so the day is

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:42.303
cut at a set time. This shape is a candle:

00:02:42.303 --> 00:02:46.963
one day of price. This candle is 19 July

00:02:46.963 --> 00:02:49.378
2023. The high, the low, and the close are

00:02:49.378 --> 00:02:52.094
labelled. A wick is the thin line that

00:02:52.094 --> 00:02:54.505
reaches up to the high or down to the low.

00:02:55.025 --> 00:02:55.474
The wick

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:56.374
shows price went

00:02:56.374 --> 00:02:56.695
there

00:02:56.695 --> 00:02:57.145
briefly,

00:02:57.145 --> 00:02:57.658
then came

00:02:57.658 --> 00:02:58.494
back before the

00:02:58.494 --> 00:02:58.686
day

00:02:58.686 --> 00:03:02.251
closed. The example is Bitcoin's public

00:03:02.251 --> 00:03:05.706
daily price in US dollars. From 19 July

00:03:05.706 --> 00:03:09.417
2023 to 16 October 2023, every one of

00:03:09.417 --> 00:03:13.776
those days closed inside the band. We do

00:03:13.776 --> 00:03:14.223
not need

00:03:14.223 --> 00:03:14.351
to

00:03:14.351 --> 00:03:14.862
read each

00:03:14.862 --> 00:03:17.411
day. The shape is the lesson, and it is

00:03:17.411 --> 00:03:20.803
marked Example. A stop is a rule you write

00:03:20.803 --> 00:03:23.010
down before you start, saying what you

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:25.287
will do if the price leaves the band and

00:03:25.287 --> 00:03:28.775
does not come back. On 23 October 2023 the

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:32.443
close finished above the top line. The

00:03:32.443 --> 00:03:32.955
price did

00:03:32.955 --> 00:03:33.402
not come

00:03:33.402 --> 00:03:36.142
back, so this example was finished. Write

00:03:36.142 --> 00:03:37.879
your stop rule down before

00:03:37.879 --> 00:03:38.061
you

00:03:38.061 --> 00:03:40.913
start. On the card it says: Stop = when

00:03:40.913 --> 00:03:46.758
you quit. Worked check: 19 July 2023 to 16

00:03:46.758 --> 00:03:51.089
October 2023. Six equal gaps of about 900

00:03:51.089 --> 00:03:54.474
dollars. The low is the bottom line. The

00:03:54.474 --> 00:03:57.874
high is the top line. The stop rule is: if

00:03:57.874 --> 00:04:00.252
the daily close leaves the top line and

00:04:00.252 --> 00:04:02.630
does not come back, the idea is finished.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.434
Nothing on this card is

00:04:04.434 --> 00:04:04.569
an

00:04:04.569 --> 00:04:07.568
order. Price often moves sideways,

00:04:07.568 --> 00:04:09.948
bouncing between the same top and bottom

00:04:09.948 --> 00:04:12.791
instead of leaving. A grid is a ladder of

00:04:12.791 --> 00:04:15.915
limit orders built for that bouncing. When

00:04:15.915 --> 00:04:17.496
price runs one way and stays

00:04:17.496 --> 00:04:17.839
there,

00:04:17.839 --> 00:04:19.352
the bot has nothing left to

00:04:19.352 --> 00:04:22.730
do. A grid has three parts you can name:

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:24.406
the range, the levels, and the

00:04:24.406 --> 00:04:27.537
stop. The range is the band. The levels

00:04:27.537 --> 00:04:27.730
are

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:28.633
the rungs inside

00:04:28.633 --> 00:04:31.999
it. Buy orders sit on lines below the

00:04:31.999 --> 00:04:34.489
price and sell orders sit on lines above

00:04:34.489 --> 00:04:37.298
it. The sells need some coin, so a grid

00:04:37.298 --> 00:04:39.833
starts with part cash and part coin, and

00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:43.298
that is a description, not advice. No

00:04:43.298 --> 00:04:43.612
order

00:04:43.612 --> 00:04:43.738
is

00:04:43.738 --> 00:04:44.241
sent from

00:04:44.241 --> 00:04:44.492
this

00:04:44.492 --> 00:04:47.634
lesson. You draw the idea. If a screen

00:04:47.634 --> 00:04:50.129
appears later, it should be a copy of the

00:04:50.129 --> 00:04:53.398
page, and only on paper or demo. The

00:04:53.398 --> 00:04:53.927
course is

00:04:53.927 --> 00:04:53.993
a

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:56.758
map, and this introduction is only the

00:04:56.758 --> 00:04:59.596
first square. Next is a checklist. Then

00:04:59.596 --> 00:04:59.814
the

00:04:59.814 --> 00:05:02.405
definition. Then calm or trending markets.

00:05:02.405 --> 00:05:02.652
Then

00:05:02.652 --> 00:05:05.473
spacing and range. Then entry and exit.

00:05:05.932 --> 00:05:06.895
Then a paper

00:05:06.895 --> 00:05:09.639
screen. Then monitoring. Then mistakes.

00:05:10.082 --> 00:05:12.679
Then scaling. Then an opt-in lesson on

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:15.938
liquidation. An order fills when price

00:05:15.938 --> 00:05:18.830
reaches its line and the trade happens. As

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:21.219
price climbs, each sell order fills, so

00:05:21.219 --> 00:05:24.121
you end up holding cash. As price falls,

00:05:24.121 --> 00:05:26.189
each buy order fills, so you end up

00:05:26.189 --> 00:05:29.560
holding coin. There is no result number in

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:29.792
this

00:05:29.792 --> 00:05:32.356
lesson. A result number would pretend the

00:05:32.356 --> 00:05:33.205
example already

00:05:33.205 --> 00:05:36.598
happened. The example is a drawing of a

00:05:36.598 --> 00:05:39.364
mechanism. The next step is the setup

00:05:39.364 --> 00:05:41.602
checklist, on paper, before any screen.

00:05:42.122 --> 00:05:42.301
You

00:05:42.301 --> 00:05:42.539
will

00:05:42.539 --> 00:05:42.777
need

00:05:42.777 --> 00:05:42.956
the

00:05:42.956 --> 00:05:43.254
three

00:05:43.254 --> 00:05:43.552
words

00:05:43.552 --> 00:05:43.790
when

00:05:43.790 --> 00:05:44.028
that

00:05:44.028 --> 00:05:44.564
checklist

00:05:44.564 --> 00:05:44.802
asks

00:05:44.802 --> 00:05:45.041
what

00:05:45.041 --> 00:05:45.100
a

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:45.338
grid

00:05:45.338 --> 00:05:48.827
is. A paper or demo account is a fence

00:05:48.827 --> 00:05:51.743
around practice. Inside the fence you can

00:05:51.743 --> 00:05:52.315
see fields

00:05:52.315 --> 00:05:52.506
and

00:05:52.506 --> 00:05:54.993
buttons. You still do not send an order in

00:05:54.993 --> 00:05:55.227
this

00:05:55.227 --> 00:05:58.673
course. If you keep one sentence, keep

00:05:58.673 --> 00:06:00.804
this: range, levels, and stop, drawn

00:06:00.804 --> 00:06:03.929
before any click. Bouncing inside the band

00:06:03.929 --> 00:06:04.715
is what a grid

00:06:04.715 --> 00:06:05.215
is built

00:06:05.215 --> 00:06:08.012
for. The exit from the band is the failure

00:06:08.012 --> 00:06:11.492
picture. A grid bot places waiting buys

00:06:11.492 --> 00:06:13.867
below the price and waiting sells above

00:06:13.867 --> 00:06:17.692
it. This 2023 path stayed between the

00:06:17.692 --> 00:06:20.351
bottom line and the top line, with six

00:06:20.351 --> 00:06:24.313
gaps of about 900 between the lines. The

00:06:24.313 --> 00:06:24.825
stop rule

00:06:24.825 --> 00:06:25.337
says what

00:06:25.337 --> 00:06:25.785
you will

00:06:25.785 --> 00:06:25.913
do

00:06:25.913 --> 00:06:26.041
if

00:06:26.041 --> 00:06:26.937
the price leaves

00:06:26.937 --> 00:06:27.385
and does

00:06:27.385 --> 00:06:27.832
not come

00:06:27.832 --> 00:06:31.121
back. Next lesson: What you are going to

00:06:31.121 --> 00:06:33.975
need. The pair is the two things you swap,

00:06:33.975 --> 00:06:36.794
like Bitcoin and US dollars. Bring your

00:06:36.794 --> 00:06:37.129
notes:

00:06:37.129 --> 00:06:37.532
the top

00:06:37.532 --> 00:06:38.271
and bottom of

00:06:38.271 --> 00:06:38.472
the

00:06:38.472 --> 00:06:41.058
band, the gaps between the lines, and your

00:06:41.058 --> 00:06:43.274
stop rule. Leave every figure marked

00:06:43.274 --> 00:06:43.767
EXAMPLE,

00:06:43.767 --> 00:06:45.859
and no order is sent between lessons.

